{"run": "digest", "t": 37799, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] Iraqi conflict — Ahmad al-Hamidawi, leader of Kata'ib Hezbollah, announces that the group will suspend military activities in Iraq following the withdrawal of U.S. troops, with the exception of targeting hostile aircraft violating the country's airspace."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 37799, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] Gaza war — Israeli settlers shoot and murder a Palestinian man at his home in Yasuf, West Bank, and injure two others. The Israeli military says that it is investigating the incident."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 37799, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] Sudanese civil war, Kordofan campaign — Five people are killed in a drone strike by the Rapid Support Forces on a dormitory at the University of Kordofan in El Obeid, North Kordofan."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 37799, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Armed conflicts and attacks] 2026 Afghanistan–Pakistan war — Pakistan launches airstrikes in Afghanistan, claiming the killing of 22 fighters at two locations, while the Government of Afghanistan reports that nine women and children are killed in Kunar Province and Helmand Province by Pakistan airstr"}
{"run": "digest", "t": 37800, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Disasters and accidents] A medical helicopter transporting a patient crashes off the coast of Santa Catalina Island in Los Angeles County, California, United States, killing two and injuring two others with one person still missing."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 37800, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [International relations] The European Commission stops payments with immediate effect to Sierra Leone, that would be €18 million for 2026, after the nations refused to cooperate with the extradition of drugs trafficker Jos Leijdekkers."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 37800, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] Sentencing Act 2026 — Hundreds of prisoners begin leaving prison in England and Wales under an early release scheme by the British government to avoid overcapacity in prisons. More than 4,500 \"low-risk\" prisoners are expected to be released in the coming weeks."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 37800, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Law and crime] Former Malawian military chief Paul Valentino Phiri is arrested by Malawi's anti-corruption agency for allegedly trafficking weapons to Sudan during his tenure in June and July 2025."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 37800, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Politics and elections] Immigration to Japan — Japan tightens permanent residency requirements for foreign nationals, introducing above-average income and basic Japanese-language standards while raising application fees twentyfold as part of broader changes to immigration policy."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 37800, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Politics and elections] Gerardo Giovagnoli and William Casali are sworn in as the new Captains Regent of San Marino, succeeding Alice Mina and Vladimiro Selva."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 37800, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Politics and elections] Ousted Sudanese leader Omar al-Bashir is sent to a military hospital in Khartoum, Sudan, for medical treatment."}
{"run": "digest", "t": 37800, "kind": "dbg", "msg": "wiki: NOT COVERED [Science and technology] SpaceX Crew-13 — The SpaceX Crew-13 mission to the International Space Station launches, carrying two NASA astronauts, one Roscosmos cosmonaut, and one Canadian Space Agency astronaut, from Cape Canaveral Space Force Station in Florida, United States."}
